1
00:00:02,469 --> 00:00:05,171
Michiko Daimon, you're fired.

2
00:00:09,609 --> 00:00:10,977
It's been a while.

3
00:00:12,178 --> 00:00:13,046
What?

4
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:15,315
Our Daimon?

5
00:00:22,922 --> 00:00:25,025
MINAMITAKAMATSU FISHING PORT

6
00:00:28,161 --> 00:00:30,430
This should be good.

7
00:00:31,631 --> 00:00:33,533
What a haul.

8
00:00:33,967 --> 00:00:35,802
It's been a while.

9
00:00:35,869 --> 00:00:38,705
Great. I want to be a fisherman.

10
00:00:38,772 --> 00:00:43,643
No way. Women can't be fishermen.

11
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:45,745
Why not?

12
00:00:49,582 --> 00:00:50,850
What's wrong, Hassaku?

13
00:00:52,619 --> 00:00:54,754
He ate too fast.

14
00:00:57,490 --> 00:00:59,225
You ate too much, I guess.

15
00:00:59,726 --> 00:01:01,061
Maybe it's the oysters.

16
00:01:01,661 --> 00:01:05,665
Drink sake
and sanitize your stomach.

17
00:01:07,901 --> 00:01:10,703
Lie down. Stop eating and help me.

18
00:01:12,839 --> 00:01:14,207
Lay him down on his back.

19
00:01:15,842 --> 00:01:16,943
I pull down your pants.

20
00:01:20,914 --> 00:01:23,616
- Where is it hurting? Here?
- No.

21
00:01:23,683 --> 00:01:24,884
- Here?
- No.

22
00:01:24,951 --> 00:01:28,855
- It's not appendicitis. Here?
- No.

23
00:01:28,922 --> 00:01:29,823
- Here?
- Yeah! Gosh!

24
00:01:33,226 --> 00:01:35,895
By the way, who are you?

25
00:01:36,763 --> 00:01:39,399
- A surgeon. Just passing by.
- A surgeon?

26
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,269
I know it hurts. But don't worry.

27
00:01:43,336 --> 00:01:46,072
Hello? The patient is 32 years old,
male,

28
00:01:46,139 --> 00:01:49,843
and he has rebound tenderness
on the upper abdominal.

29
00:01:50,477 --> 00:01:54,914
Can be perforation of the stomach.
Prepare for surgery. Don't swing.

30
00:01:54,981 --> 00:01:56,049
Keep the position.

31
00:01:56,816 --> 00:01:58,718
Miss, you're so cool.

32
00:01:58,785 --> 00:02:02,088
You lead us at the front
like an ambulance.

33
00:02:02,155 --> 00:02:03,423
You've got it.

34
00:02:11,898 --> 00:02:12,765
Hang in there!

35
00:02:12,832 --> 00:02:15,268
TEITO MEDICAL UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL
24TH BRANCH

36
00:02:15,335 --> 00:02:17,737
CT-scan him. Then do a gastroscopy.

37
00:02:17,804 --> 00:02:21,508
- Hey, who are you?
- Me?

38
00:02:21,574 --> 00:02:24,677
- She's a surgeon.
- That's correct.

39
00:02:24,744 --> 00:02:26,112
Get out of our way.

40
00:02:26,179 --> 00:02:27,013
Hurry up, hurry.

41
00:02:28,348 --> 00:02:29,282
Let's start.

42
00:02:29,349 --> 00:02:31,050
Performing distal gastrectomy.

43
00:02:31,117 --> 00:02:32,819
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

44
00:02:36,756 --> 00:02:40,460
- Oh my gosh, Daimon!
- Hello.

45
00:02:42,028 --> 00:02:44,264
- What are you doing?
- Can't you see?

46
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:47,033
Why are you in Takamatsu branch?

47
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:48,234
Focus on your hands.

48
00:02:48,301 --> 00:02:50,837
You guys are listening to her.

49
00:02:50,904 --> 00:02:52,572
- Suction.
- Yes, ma'am.

50
00:02:56,743 --> 00:02:58,378
I never fail.

51
00:02:58,444 --> 00:03:01,281
That's not my point.

52
00:03:01,347 --> 00:03:03,816
- This is good.
- Answer me.

53
00:03:03,883 --> 00:03:06,319
That operation was not my plan.

54
00:03:06,386 --> 00:03:09,622
You asked the headquarters
to send good doctors here.

55
00:03:09,689 --> 00:03:12,225
- No, we didn't.
- Don't lie.

56
00:03:12,292 --> 00:03:14,360
This tiny hospital can't afford

57
00:03:14,427 --> 00:03:16,329
to hire a doctor like you.

58
00:03:16,396 --> 00:03:19,032
But I was called to come here.

59
00:03:22,635 --> 00:03:23,603
It has to be a mistake.

60
00:03:25,038 --> 00:03:27,473
Timing was good. I was unemployed.

61
00:03:28,541 --> 00:03:29,375
Unemployed?

62
00:03:31,377 --> 00:03:35,648
I didn't perform surgery last week.
I wanted to do it so badly.

63
00:03:35,715 --> 00:03:37,617
You're unemployed?

64
00:03:38,518 --> 00:03:40,119
You finally lost your touch, huh.

65
00:03:40,186 --> 00:03:41,854
- Medical mistake?
- No way.

66
00:03:42,488 --> 00:03:46,459
The head's wife of the fishery
association gave them to me.

67
00:03:46,526 --> 00:03:49,562
- You get used to be here.
- I had to.

68
00:03:52,131 --> 00:03:53,600
This mandarin is so good.

69
00:03:53,666 --> 00:03:57,003
You know why I was relocated here.

70
00:03:57,403 --> 00:04:00,506
If you were not there,
I would have...

71
00:04:00,573 --> 00:04:02,242
A chairperson?

72
00:04:02,308 --> 00:04:04,744
Of course, I would have.

73
00:04:10,016 --> 00:04:10,984
Speaking of that,

74
00:04:11,517 --> 00:04:15,722
the chairperson's election
of Teito University is coming soon.

75
00:04:16,289 --> 00:04:18,424
The medical staff must be so hectic.

76
00:04:19,025 --> 00:04:21,327
Medical staff... Election...

77
00:04:22,428 --> 00:04:25,999
Those sound really nice.
It brings back memories.

78
00:04:26,065 --> 00:04:30,870
Cash bundles are everywhere
in the university hospital.

79
00:04:30,937 --> 00:04:35,008
Only mandarins are found
in such a local hospital...

80
00:04:35,074 --> 00:04:35,942
You idiot!

81
00:04:36,009 --> 00:04:37,877
Pay me the mandarin fee.

82
00:04:37,944 --> 00:04:39,646
You stay the same.

83
00:04:46,853 --> 00:04:51,291
Well, these three candidates run
for the chairperson's election

84
00:04:51,824 --> 00:04:56,596
of the 2nd surgery department
at Teito University Hospital.

85
00:04:56,663 --> 00:04:59,232
<i>University hospitals lost</i>
<i>their authorities.</i>

86
00:04:59,299 --> 00:05:01,634
<i>Medical care has become a world</i>

87
00:05:01,701 --> 00:05:05,338
<i>where the strong prey on the weak.</i>

88
00:05:05,405 --> 00:05:11,644
While Dr. Takano came back here
at the last moment,

89
00:05:11,711 --> 00:05:14,647
Dr. Kondo was unexpectedly
selected as a candidate.

90
00:05:15,014 --> 00:05:19,786
Dr. Ebina has a weak presence,
contrary to his scary face.

91
00:05:22,889 --> 00:05:25,158
TAKASHI EBINA

92
00:05:25,224 --> 00:05:26,893
SHINOBU KONDO

93
00:05:28,328 --> 00:05:32,699
<i>To save this crisis in the world of</i>
<i>medical care, a freelance doctor,</i>

94
00:05:33,866 --> 00:05:37,236
<i>in another word,</i>
<i>a maverick doctor, appeared.</i>

95
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:44,811
Kurumi, go back.

96
00:05:44,877 --> 00:05:46,813
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

97
00:05:49,649 --> 00:05:50,683
Surgeon!

98
00:05:50,750 --> 00:05:53,152
<i>She hates groups, authority,</i>

99
00:05:53,219 --> 00:05:54,654
<i>and being controlled.</i>

100
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:57,190
Are you a patient?

101
00:05:57,957 --> 00:06:03,096
<i>Her medical certifications</i>
<i>and work experience are her only weapons.</i>

102
00:06:03,162 --> 00:06:06,265
Kurumi, you have to
get an IV drip today.

103
00:06:06,332 --> 00:06:07,300
I don't want it.

104
00:06:07,867 --> 00:06:08,901
Kurumi.

105
00:06:10,837 --> 00:06:13,639
It'll be done quickly
if you calm down.

106
00:06:13,706 --> 00:06:16,142
Thanks. Let's go.

107
00:06:19,312 --> 00:06:20,680
What is her disease?

108
00:06:20,747 --> 00:06:23,116
Malignant myofibroblastic sarcoma.

109
00:06:23,182 --> 00:06:26,085
Sarcoma? Is it big?

110
00:06:26,152 --> 00:06:27,186
About 15cm.

111
00:06:28,154 --> 00:06:29,489
15cm?

112
00:06:29,555 --> 00:06:34,127
It's on abdominal aorta,
and it coils around the vessels.

113
00:06:36,963 --> 00:06:38,965
The headquarters had her once.

114
00:06:39,565 --> 00:06:42,368
But they found
no other means to cure her.

115
00:06:42,902 --> 00:06:44,337
Then she was returned here.

116
00:06:45,405 --> 00:06:46,305
What's the plan?

117
00:06:46,672 --> 00:06:47,974
What's the plan?

118
00:06:48,541 --> 00:06:53,179
Even you understand it's impossible
to perform surgery on her.

119
00:06:54,781 --> 00:06:59,252
All I could do is to give her
steroid IV and chemotherapy.

120
00:07:00,386 --> 00:07:01,421
Her parents wish

121
00:07:02,121 --> 00:07:06,826
she will die in her hometown.

122
00:07:09,195 --> 00:07:11,130
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

123
00:07:11,898 --> 00:07:14,901
<i>also as known as Doctor-X.</i>

124
00:07:25,845 --> 00:07:28,748
Tsumo! Junchan-sansiki-dora-ichi!

125
00:07:29,715 --> 00:07:32,351
No way! You've had damaten?

126
00:07:32,785 --> 00:07:34,020
I won three hands in a row.

127
00:07:35,521 --> 00:07:38,624
Hiromi, you're getting better.

128
00:07:38,691 --> 00:07:40,159
Thanks to you.

129
00:07:40,693 --> 00:07:43,796
So Daimon went to Takamatsu?

130
00:07:43,863 --> 00:07:46,532
She performed
the operation for Prof. Takano.

131
00:07:46,933 --> 00:07:51,404
That means she had joined
Executive Manger Mabuchi's side?

132
00:07:51,471 --> 00:07:53,172
Exactly.

133
00:07:53,239 --> 00:07:56,175
- Takano, you're working hard.
- Thank you.

134
00:07:57,009 --> 00:07:59,779
You'll win
the chairperson's election.

135
00:08:00,246 --> 00:08:03,416
- I'm not sure of that yet.
- Yes, you will.

136
00:08:03,883 --> 00:08:05,418
I hope so, too.

137
00:08:05,485 --> 00:08:07,887
The other candidates run for it too.

138
00:08:09,655 --> 00:08:12,959
Prof. Hiruma is so upset.

139
00:08:14,427 --> 00:08:17,463
What are you going to do?
I'm asking you two.

140
00:08:18,064 --> 00:08:22,969
Takano is leading.
Do you understand?

141
00:08:23,436 --> 00:08:25,605
I heard they bribe a lot.

142
00:08:25,671 --> 00:08:27,240
- You heard?
- Sorry.

143
00:08:27,306 --> 00:08:31,944
We've got to win
over the undecided voters.

144
00:08:32,011 --> 00:08:35,681
Invite them to
steak or grilled eels dinner.

145
00:08:35,748 --> 00:08:39,051
Omiya Sukiyabashi
in the main building for steak?

146
00:08:39,118 --> 00:08:41,254
- It doesn't matter!
- No, sir.

147
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:43,122
- Even puffer fish is fine.
- Pufferfish?

148
00:08:43,189 --> 00:08:45,458
That's not my point, idiot!

149
00:08:45,525 --> 00:08:47,059
- Yes, sir.
- Stand there!

150
00:08:47,126 --> 00:08:48,828
Executive Manager Hiruma!

151
00:08:49,328 --> 00:08:51,631
Oh, it's a good timing.

152
00:08:51,697 --> 00:08:54,800
What's the name
of the eel restaurant in Ginza...

153
00:08:54,867 --> 00:08:56,469
This is an emergency.

154
00:08:56,536 --> 00:08:57,737
What happened?

155
00:08:57,803 --> 00:09:01,173
We've just had an urgent patient.

156
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:04,810
It happens on a daily basis.

157
00:09:04,877 --> 00:09:07,146
Executive Manager Mabuchi

158
00:09:08,381 --> 00:09:10,383
and Prof. Takano
are examining the patient.

159
00:09:10,449 --> 00:09:12,985
I see. So what's the problem?

160
00:09:13,052 --> 00:09:15,254
Who is the patient?

161
00:09:17,857 --> 00:09:21,394
That's... So...

162
00:09:21,460 --> 00:09:23,663
So? Who is it?

163
00:09:24,764 --> 00:09:25,631
Hiruma...

164
00:09:27,700 --> 00:09:28,668
Me?

165
00:09:32,772 --> 00:09:35,074
Oh, everyone is here.

166
00:09:35,942 --> 00:09:36,943
Excuse me.

167
00:09:37,910 --> 00:09:42,014
YUKAKO HIRUMA, HIRUMA'S DAUGHTER

168
00:09:42,081 --> 00:09:44,050
Yuka? Yuka?

169
00:09:45,151 --> 00:09:45,985
Oh my!

170
00:09:51,157 --> 00:09:52,024
Kondo.

171
00:10:10,376 --> 00:10:12,478
Sorry, but please leave us alone.

172
00:10:14,547 --> 00:10:15,514
Get out now!

173
00:10:16,816 --> 00:10:17,717
Excuse us.

174
00:10:29,929 --> 00:10:34,500
Her melanoma has come back.

175
00:10:36,068 --> 00:10:37,069
Yuka...

176
00:10:37,136 --> 00:10:41,240
The 5cm mass was found
on a caudate lobe of

177
00:10:41,307 --> 00:10:43,776
Prof. Hiruma's daughter.

178
00:10:45,277 --> 00:10:48,280
It can be metastasis
of malignant melanoma.

179
00:10:50,783 --> 00:10:53,586
The condition is critical.

180
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:55,821
It requires prompt action.

181
00:10:57,323 --> 00:10:58,924
But our surgical department

182
00:11:00,359 --> 00:11:03,062
can't do this operation on her.

183
00:11:06,365 --> 00:11:10,002
At St. Hopkins Hospital
in the United States,

184
00:11:10,302 --> 00:11:12,738
a few surgery for the same case

185
00:11:12,805 --> 00:11:15,675
were successful
by caudate lobectomy.

186
00:11:16,242 --> 00:11:19,779
In the United States?
Caudate lobectomy?

187
00:11:20,746 --> 00:11:25,084
Contact St. Hopkins Hospital
and make an appointment

188
00:11:25,718 --> 00:11:27,286
for her surgery.

189
00:11:27,353 --> 00:11:28,487
Sure.

190
00:11:28,554 --> 00:11:30,222
Excuse me, everyone.

191
00:11:31,857 --> 00:11:36,696
Thanks for your concern.
Sorry that I lost my temper before.

192
00:11:38,264 --> 00:11:39,298
We will...

193
00:11:41,734 --> 00:11:44,136
- perform this surgery here.
- But...

194
00:11:44,203 --> 00:11:45,037
Professor Takano,

195
00:11:46,138 --> 00:11:50,876
I'm the executive manager of
the surgery department in this hospital.

196
00:11:50,943 --> 00:11:55,247
Instead of letting my daughter have
surgery here, we'll send her away.

197
00:11:55,314 --> 00:11:56,382
How dare you?

198
00:11:57,149 --> 00:11:59,118
What a shame!

199
00:12:03,155 --> 00:12:06,459
Put aside your ego. Come on.

200
00:12:06,926 --> 00:12:08,728
- Ebina.
- Yes?

201
00:12:10,763 --> 00:12:12,198
You do this operation.

202
00:12:15,234 --> 00:12:16,535
Why the hesitation?

203
00:12:17,970 --> 00:12:21,574
What about your usual "Yes, sir?"

204
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:22,475
Sorry.

205
00:12:24,977 --> 00:12:26,278
What about you, Kondo?

206
00:12:28,280 --> 00:12:29,115
Sir?

207
00:12:30,015 --> 00:12:31,517
Depending on your answer,

208
00:12:31,984 --> 00:12:35,821
I will eliminate the other
two candidates for the election.

209
00:12:37,923 --> 00:12:38,858
Can you do it?

210
00:12:43,262 --> 00:12:45,998
Caudate lobectomy...

211
00:12:47,967 --> 00:12:51,504
Have you conducted
the caudate lobectomy?

212
00:12:52,371 --> 00:12:53,339
Can you do that?

213
00:12:55,608 --> 00:12:56,609
No, sir...

214
00:12:56,675 --> 00:13:00,713
Don't utter a sound
if you can't do it!

215
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:01,680
I'm very sorry.

216
00:13:08,387 --> 00:13:09,889
Can anyone do it?

217
00:13:11,824 --> 00:13:12,658
I'm sorry.

218
00:13:13,526 --> 00:13:14,460
Shame on you all!

219
00:13:14,927 --> 00:13:15,895
Yes, sir!

220
00:13:17,530 --> 00:13:18,631
Now you say that.

221
00:13:18,697 --> 00:13:19,732
I'm sorry.

222
00:13:20,366 --> 00:13:22,334
In such a loud voice...

223
00:13:23,035 --> 00:13:24,036
I'm sorry.

224
00:13:26,539 --> 00:13:27,506
Prof. Ebina.

225
00:13:28,607 --> 00:13:29,441
What is it?

226
00:13:29,942 --> 00:13:31,677
This can be the opportunity.

227
00:13:32,678 --> 00:13:33,512
The opportunity?

228
00:13:33,846 --> 00:13:36,549
If you succeed in Yukako's surgery,

229
00:13:36,615 --> 00:13:39,852
Prof. Hiruma will endorse you 100%.

230
00:13:41,854 --> 00:13:44,690
How did you guys know that?
This is confidential.

231
00:13:45,157 --> 00:13:47,526
Power of our information network.

232
00:13:47,593 --> 00:13:49,762
You know whom we work for.

233
00:13:50,596 --> 00:13:54,834
If it works, not only you will become
a chairperson, you will have it made.

234
00:14:00,172 --> 00:14:01,006
What if I fail?

235
00:14:04,043 --> 00:14:06,478
You won't be just sent away.

236
00:14:13,853 --> 00:14:16,388
I was sent away here because of you.

237
00:14:16,689 --> 00:14:18,524
My life is totally a mess.

238
00:14:18,591 --> 00:14:19,725
Wait, Kaji.

239
00:14:19,792 --> 00:14:21,727
You can't trick me.

240
00:14:21,794 --> 00:14:23,195
About Kurumi's surgery.

241
00:14:23,262 --> 00:14:26,799
How about stopping
the blood's flow near the mass?

242
00:14:26,866 --> 00:14:29,201
It' won't be enough time.

243
00:14:29,668 --> 00:14:32,705
The tumor is in the organ and the vessels.

244
00:14:33,839 --> 00:14:36,408
How about a temporary bypass?

245
00:14:36,475 --> 00:14:39,311
It won't interrupt the blood flows.

246
00:14:39,378 --> 00:14:41,313
The tumor invades abdominal aorta,

247
00:14:41,380 --> 00:14:44,183
vena cava, mesenteric artery,
and celiac artery.

248
00:14:44,250 --> 00:14:45,951
How can I perform surgery?

249
00:14:47,319 --> 00:14:49,054
Let's see...

250
00:14:50,756 --> 00:14:52,191
Here's Kurumi's records.

251
00:14:53,359 --> 00:14:56,061
If the world went right,
or if you didn't show up,

252
00:14:56,528 --> 00:14:59,398
I'd have become a chairperson.

253
00:14:59,465 --> 00:15:02,534
And I've concluded
the surgery was impossible.

254
00:15:03,769 --> 00:15:05,437
Don't take my word light.

255
00:15:09,775 --> 00:15:11,110
I'm frustrated, too.

256
00:15:17,116 --> 00:15:18,517
YUKAKO HIRUMA, AGE 9

257
00:15:47,813 --> 00:15:49,148
Dr. Kondo.

258
00:15:50,916 --> 00:15:53,719
Will I be okay?

259
00:15:57,923 --> 00:15:58,791
Yes, you will.

260
00:16:03,829 --> 00:16:04,964
I don't want to die.

261
00:16:13,639 --> 00:16:16,875
My dad came here and said,

262
00:16:18,277 --> 00:16:21,947
"You'll get well. We will cure you."

263
00:16:25,617 --> 00:16:29,922
You will perform surgery
on me, right?

264
00:16:32,958 --> 00:16:33,959
I want

265
00:16:36,328 --> 00:16:38,263
you to save my life.

266
00:16:44,236 --> 00:16:47,773
LISA HASHIMOTO, NURSE

267
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:48,941
That's right.

268
00:16:50,109 --> 00:16:53,112
Dr. Kondo will save your life.

269
00:17:10,896 --> 00:17:12,631
SHINOBU KONDO'S OFFICE

270
00:17:16,702 --> 00:17:19,872
Caudate lobectomy...

271
00:17:26,545 --> 00:17:30,282
"Our expert team
of St. Hopkins University

272
00:17:31,417 --> 00:17:33,919
has succeeded in the surgery of

273
00:17:34,386 --> 00:17:40,125
malignant melanoma metastasis,
which was difficult to perform."

274
00:17:41,460 --> 00:17:45,030
"In this surgery,
one of our team members

275
00:17:45,497 --> 00:17:48,333
provided strong leadership

276
00:17:48,767 --> 00:17:52,871
and led this caudate lobectomy
to the success..."

277
00:18:01,313 --> 00:18:02,548
"It was Doctor-X."

278
00:18:17,496 --> 00:18:20,599
See? That's my dad.

279
00:18:20,666 --> 00:18:21,533
Which one?

280
00:18:22,167 --> 00:18:24,503
The blue one. Dad!

281
00:18:24,570 --> 00:18:25,904
Good job!

282
00:18:27,906 --> 00:18:28,907
Hey, Kurumi!

283
00:18:29,641 --> 00:18:30,809
Wow, he's handsome.

284
00:18:35,547 --> 00:18:39,551
If I were a boy, I could become
a fisherman like my dad.

285
00:18:39,618 --> 00:18:42,254
You can still be a fisherman.

286
00:18:43,755 --> 00:18:44,857
But...

287
00:18:48,127 --> 00:18:51,163
If I can't become an adult,
I can't be.

288
00:19:03,308 --> 00:19:04,576
Dad.

289
00:19:05,911 --> 00:19:08,213
We've caught plenty today.

290
00:19:18,924 --> 00:19:20,359
Hello, Akira?

291
00:19:20,425 --> 00:19:24,563
Oh my, is it telepathy?
I was going to call you.

292
00:19:25,197 --> 00:19:26,064
What is it?

293
00:19:26,131 --> 00:19:28,333
Michiko, come back right now.

294
00:19:29,234 --> 00:19:32,037
We have a confidential offer.

295
00:19:32,104 --> 00:19:33,338
Confidential?

296
00:19:33,405 --> 00:19:37,042
Doesn't it sound fancy?
Confidential, confidential.

297
00:19:38,810 --> 00:19:41,013
- You mean it smells money.
- Exactly.

298
00:19:41,313 --> 00:19:44,583
The payment is 10 times more
than usual.

299
00:19:46,018 --> 00:19:47,719
Wow. So where should I go?

300
00:19:47,786 --> 00:19:51,123
2nd Surgery Dept. of
Teito Medical University Hospital.

301
00:19:51,924 --> 00:19:53,058
I won't go back.

302
00:19:53,125 --> 00:19:55,394
Hiruma's daughter

303
00:19:55,460 --> 00:19:59,264
has metastasis of
malignant melanoma on caudate lobe.

304
00:20:00,199 --> 00:20:01,366
Metastasis on caudate lobe?

305
00:20:01,433 --> 00:20:05,137
Teito's doctors can't
perform surgery on her.

306
00:20:07,472 --> 00:20:09,274
Metastasis?

307
00:20:09,341 --> 00:20:11,210
You did this operation in the U.S.,

308
00:20:11,610 --> 00:20:13,579
the caudate lobectomy.

309
00:20:15,380 --> 00:20:18,250
- Oh yeah, I did that.
- I know you can do it.

310
00:20:22,821 --> 00:20:23,989
Aren't you excited?

311
00:20:25,924 --> 00:20:27,759
Go for it, Dad.

312
00:20:36,101 --> 00:20:41,139
It is sudden,
but I'm going back to Tokyo.

313
00:20:41,873 --> 00:20:42,741
What?

314
00:20:43,842 --> 00:20:44,676
Hey,

315
00:20:46,678 --> 00:20:48,447
don't give up on yourself.

316
00:20:50,582 --> 00:20:53,018
You'll be a fisherman, won't you?

317
00:20:54,486 --> 00:20:55,387
I want to.

318
00:20:56,755 --> 00:20:57,823
Then promise me.

319
00:20:58,857 --> 00:21:01,526
Don't give up.

320
00:21:07,165 --> 00:21:08,000
Say okay.

321
00:21:09,601 --> 00:21:10,469
Alright.

322
00:21:11,069 --> 00:21:14,706
Well, let's go back
and get you an IV drip.

323
00:21:18,910 --> 00:21:22,147
Did she already quit here
and go back to Tokyo?

324
00:21:23,282 --> 00:21:25,284
She was just passing by.

325
00:21:25,350 --> 00:21:26,451
That woman

326
00:21:27,085 --> 00:21:31,056
follows the smell of money after all.

327
00:21:35,294 --> 00:21:38,597
I'm thinking of going home in Tokyo

328
00:21:39,598 --> 00:21:41,266
so as to introduce you to my mom.

329
00:21:43,335 --> 00:21:46,371
My wife wants the American hospital

330
00:21:47,506 --> 00:21:50,475
to perform surgery on our daughter.

331
00:21:51,443 --> 00:21:52,344
As for myself,

332
00:21:53,679 --> 00:21:59,318
we should do that at our hospital.

333
00:21:59,685 --> 00:22:03,088
For saving the honor
of Teito Medical Hospital as well.

334
00:22:03,155 --> 00:22:04,656
The honor my neck.

335
00:22:05,257 --> 00:22:07,559
Just send her to the United States.

336
00:22:10,128 --> 00:22:16,134
You will be her surgeon,
right, Kondo?

337
00:22:16,201 --> 00:22:19,137
Yes, sir. Our team will do.

338
00:22:20,005 --> 00:22:22,007
Our team?

339
00:22:23,375 --> 00:22:28,947
Do you have the doctor's double?

340
00:22:29,414 --> 00:22:30,582
- Yes, sir.
- I see.

341
00:22:33,518 --> 00:22:36,321
I will never hear about it
in the future?

342
00:22:36,722 --> 00:22:37,589
No, sir.

343
00:22:38,323 --> 00:22:41,860
- Can I have one more sirloin?
- Sure.

344
00:22:44,996 --> 00:22:46,431
It's so yummy!

345
00:22:47,666 --> 00:22:52,237
Will I meet that

346
00:22:53,872 --> 00:22:54,973
talented doctor?

347
00:22:56,208 --> 00:22:57,075
No, sir.

348
00:23:00,912 --> 00:23:06,451
The doctor's double you mentioned...

349
00:23:08,153 --> 00:23:12,391
I heard she loves meat.

350
00:23:12,457 --> 00:23:16,294
I told her to eat meat
as much as she wants.

351
00:23:16,361 --> 00:23:20,165
Excuse me. I'd like to
have two more sirloins.

352
00:23:20,232 --> 00:23:21,299
Sure. Thanks.

353
00:23:22,801 --> 00:23:23,902
If...

354
00:23:25,137 --> 00:23:27,539
If the doctor I'll never see

355
00:23:27,606 --> 00:23:30,809
shows any unconfident manner,

356
00:23:32,110 --> 00:23:33,745
I'll send Yukako to America.

357
00:23:37,115 --> 00:23:38,083
No worries.

358
00:23:38,717 --> 00:23:41,019
- She never fails.
- ...never fails.

359
00:23:48,160 --> 00:23:49,060
If

360
00:23:50,462 --> 00:23:55,233
I asked the doctor's double

361
00:23:55,300 --> 00:23:58,303
to perform surgery on my daughter,

362
00:23:58,370 --> 00:24:04,209
I'm afraid how much it would cost.

363
00:24:26,465 --> 00:24:27,332
Can I fold it?

364
00:24:32,037 --> 00:24:33,872
Well, we should get going.

365
00:24:34,606 --> 00:24:37,576
Kondo, I'm counting on you.

366
00:24:40,011 --> 00:24:41,913
Let's have soba tonight.

367
00:24:41,980 --> 00:24:44,449
- Soba?
- Don't be disappointed.

368
00:24:45,050 --> 00:24:46,518
Here, sirloin.

369
00:24:49,421 --> 00:24:53,124
Thanks again for taking this case.

370
00:24:53,191 --> 00:24:54,192
No problem.

371
00:24:55,794 --> 00:25:00,699
Whatever it takes, I want to
win the chairperson's election.

372
00:25:01,900 --> 00:25:02,734
Why?

373
00:25:03,735 --> 00:25:05,737
Why is that so important to you?

374
00:25:10,208 --> 00:25:14,045
I just want to
see the view from the top.

375
00:25:25,457 --> 00:25:28,026
Now you're having a meat bun?

376
00:25:28,093 --> 00:25:29,628
This is my dessert.

377
00:25:30,428 --> 00:25:34,132
But you're a surgeon, too.

378
00:25:34,199 --> 00:25:37,769
Don't you want to do the surgery?
The patient is your fiance.

379
00:25:38,436 --> 00:25:40,205
I cannot fail.

380
00:25:41,573 --> 00:25:43,575
Any surgery should not be failed.

381
00:25:43,909 --> 00:25:46,111
So, I never fail.

382
00:25:46,678 --> 00:25:48,613
Why are you so confident?

383
00:25:48,680 --> 00:25:49,614
Let me ask you.

384
00:25:49,681 --> 00:25:53,885
Is it forgivable
if doctors make any mistake?

385
00:25:56,721 --> 00:25:59,524
Doctors must not make any mistake.

386
00:26:00,692 --> 00:26:01,560
Speaking honestly,

387
00:26:02,193 --> 00:26:06,031
I've failed the similar surgery before.

388
00:26:10,769 --> 00:26:13,939
The patient died.

389
00:26:17,509 --> 00:26:18,343
I see.

390
00:26:20,612 --> 00:26:24,583
I don't want to fail,
so I perform surgery.

391
00:26:24,649 --> 00:26:28,653
And you don't want to fail,
so you don't perform surgery.

392
00:26:29,354 --> 00:26:30,322
That's it.

393
00:26:45,503 --> 00:26:47,205
I'm ogre.

394
00:26:48,373 --> 00:26:52,510
Daimon is going to be the double?
That kind of job exists.

395
00:26:52,577 --> 00:26:55,747
This is so lucrative.
We'll have big money.

396
00:26:56,648 --> 00:26:57,849
I'm home.

397
00:26:57,916 --> 00:27:01,186
- Welcome back, the Double.
- Welcome back.

398
00:27:02,554 --> 00:27:04,489
Can you become my anesthetist?

399
00:27:04,556 --> 00:27:09,361
Sure.
But the caudate lobectomy is tough.

400
00:27:09,427 --> 00:27:10,428
Don't worry.

401
00:27:10,495 --> 00:27:14,566
I know Michiko's skills
more than she does.

402
00:27:14,633 --> 00:27:16,768
- Oh yeah?
- I'm sure you can do it.

403
00:27:18,370 --> 00:27:20,171
The Double is going to bed.

404
00:27:20,238 --> 00:27:22,073
Good night.

405
00:27:23,174 --> 00:27:25,110
Hey, what is the Double?

406
00:27:26,878 --> 00:27:31,082
- I heard it's good.
- I want to eat it, too.

407
00:27:31,149 --> 00:27:33,218
You want to eat it? How about this?

408
00:27:34,786 --> 00:27:35,620
I made this...

409
00:27:44,295 --> 00:27:47,932
Prof. Kondo. I heard you're
in charge of a special patient.

410
00:27:47,999 --> 00:27:49,834
Everybody is talking about it.

411
00:27:51,136 --> 00:27:53,104
Who's the patient?

412
00:27:53,471 --> 00:27:55,006
No spectator is allowed.

413
00:27:55,073 --> 00:27:58,143
Sorry, I can't tell you anything.

414
00:28:03,481 --> 00:28:04,582
Excuse me.

415
00:28:07,686 --> 00:28:08,720
Can I talk to you?

416
00:28:15,160 --> 00:28:18,096
Only professors and
the assigned staff

417
00:28:19,230 --> 00:28:22,467
know about today's operation.

418
00:28:24,169 --> 00:28:25,070
It seems like it.

419
00:28:27,372 --> 00:28:28,873
Do you think you can do it?

420
00:28:35,947 --> 00:28:37,716
When I have to gamble in my life,

421
00:28:39,050 --> 00:28:39,951
I will do so.

422
00:28:40,885 --> 00:28:43,855
Doctors are not gamblers.

423
00:28:47,192 --> 00:28:48,026
I know.

424
00:28:49,627 --> 00:28:53,098
It looks a reckless gamble to me.

425
00:29:00,238 --> 00:29:01,072
Kondo.

426
00:29:04,576 --> 00:29:05,910
What if you fail?

427
00:29:07,946 --> 00:29:09,848
None of doctors are allowed

428
00:29:11,683 --> 00:29:12,517
to fail.

429
00:29:26,831 --> 00:29:28,366
I see the plot.

430
00:29:28,800 --> 00:29:30,168
What do you mean?

431
00:29:30,235 --> 00:29:33,104
Michiko Daimon has come back.

432
00:29:33,772 --> 00:29:34,639
Oh?

433
00:29:35,406 --> 00:29:36,741
Don't you see?

434
00:29:38,710 --> 00:29:40,512
Is Michiko Daimon going to

435
00:29:42,113 --> 00:29:43,948
perform surgery on behalf of Kondo?

436
00:29:44,015 --> 00:29:45,350
Hiruma does whatever

437
00:29:45,683 --> 00:29:49,754
he needs
to save this hospital's honor

438
00:29:50,522 --> 00:29:52,891
and let Kondo win the election.

439
00:29:54,759 --> 00:29:55,593
What should we do?

440
00:29:56,327 --> 00:29:58,963
Are we going to
leak this case to public?

441
00:30:00,365 --> 00:30:01,199
We'd better not.

442
00:30:04,469 --> 00:30:10,575
I also have to save the honor
of Teito Medical Hospital.

443
00:30:28,560 --> 00:30:29,494
Excuse me.

444
00:30:31,229 --> 00:30:33,298
- How's Dr. Daimon?
- She's not here yet.

445
00:30:34,032 --> 00:30:34,866
I see.

446
00:30:37,435 --> 00:30:41,339
Are you sure
you can't do this operation?

447
00:30:43,374 --> 00:30:44,642
Yukako

448
00:30:45,210 --> 00:30:49,113
believes you'll do that.

449
00:31:08,366 --> 00:31:10,735
Are you really sure

450
00:31:11,469 --> 00:31:13,037
the freelance can do it?

451
00:31:14,205 --> 00:31:15,039
Don't worry.

452
00:31:17,775 --> 00:31:20,578
This is our daughter's surgery.

453
00:31:21,246 --> 00:31:22,747
Don't worry.

454
00:31:23,681 --> 00:31:24,515
You know.

455
00:31:25,850 --> 00:31:29,354
Can you ask the American team
to come over here

456
00:31:30,021 --> 00:31:32,690
and do the surgery secretly?

457
00:31:36,628 --> 00:31:39,697
- Honey.
- It should be fine.

458
00:31:49,841 --> 00:31:52,343
Hello? This is Hiruma. Karasumaru?

459
00:31:55,179 --> 00:31:59,417
Yes, it's me.
I'm waiting at the airport.

460
00:32:00,285 --> 00:32:03,955
I see. I'm just checking up on you.

461
00:32:05,123 --> 00:32:07,158
Please don't worry.

462
00:32:07,458 --> 00:32:11,095
I'll do as I'm exactly told.

463
00:32:11,529 --> 00:32:12,363
Thanks.

464
00:32:15,733 --> 00:32:18,069
- Honey!
- Don't worry.

465
00:32:37,889 --> 00:32:41,492
Epidural anesthesia and full
anesthesia makes her stable.

466
00:32:44,429 --> 00:32:46,364
Well, let's start

467
00:32:46,431 --> 00:32:50,969
the caudate lobectomy.

468
00:32:51,035 --> 00:32:53,204
Thanks, Dr. Daimon.

469
00:32:53,705 --> 00:32:54,872
Scalpel.

470
00:33:11,022 --> 00:33:11,990
Monopolar.

471
00:33:23,668 --> 00:33:25,570
- Hello.
- Hi.

472
00:33:27,405 --> 00:33:29,574
They're still operating.

473
00:33:29,874 --> 00:33:35,380
This is Daimon's special project.

474
00:33:35,446 --> 00:33:36,881
10 MILLION YEN AS OPERATION FEE

475
00:33:36,948 --> 00:33:39,250
For the Doctor Double,

476
00:33:39,317 --> 00:33:44,789
it costs extra charge.

477
00:33:45,423 --> 00:33:47,225
You're taking advantage of it.

478
00:33:47,291 --> 00:33:48,993
The payment is quite high.

479
00:33:49,394 --> 00:33:54,565
I thought I should pass the bill
on to you in advance.

480
00:33:55,533 --> 00:33:57,769
- Here you go.
- Okay.

481
00:34:03,107 --> 00:34:05,977
Of course, I brought a melon too.

482
00:34:06,377 --> 00:34:07,645
Thanks.

483
00:34:08,713 --> 00:34:12,450
But it's weird.

484
00:34:13,151 --> 00:34:18,723
Michiko Daimon directly
gave the bill to me.

485
00:34:19,690 --> 00:34:21,492
- What? She did?
- Yes.

486
00:34:22,527 --> 00:34:24,429
Well, well, well.

487
00:34:24,929 --> 00:34:27,932
I was amazed by her trick.

488
00:34:28,399 --> 00:34:31,469
She's surely something.

489
00:34:31,836 --> 00:34:32,670
May I see it?

490
00:34:39,977 --> 00:34:42,580
- Kelly.
- Retractor.

491
00:34:53,057 --> 00:34:54,826
Inferior vena cava is detached.

492
00:34:55,927 --> 00:34:58,229
CVP is under 5, and she's stable.

493
00:34:59,097 --> 00:35:00,531
Dissect short hepatic vein.

494
00:35:00,598 --> 00:35:03,067
- Pean 3/0 silk, two.
- Yes, sir.

495
00:35:09,841 --> 00:35:10,875
Metzen.

496
00:35:11,843 --> 00:35:13,678
- Sweat.
- Excuse me.

497
00:35:14,278 --> 00:35:19,550
Michiko... What is she thinking?

498
00:35:20,585 --> 00:35:22,687
Well, Give me back that bill.

499
00:35:24,322 --> 00:35:28,359
And I return this bill
of 10 million yen to you.

500
00:35:29,627 --> 00:35:32,230
Oh boy. Michiko Daimon

501
00:35:32,296 --> 00:35:36,267
is such a greedy doctor.

502
00:35:37,301 --> 00:35:39,837
I've never heard such a deal.

503
00:35:40,371 --> 00:35:42,974
Damn you, Michiko...

504
00:35:46,377 --> 00:35:49,247
Separating left caudate lobe
from ductus venosus. Mosquito.

505
00:35:50,948 --> 00:35:52,517
SURGERY TIME

506
00:35:54,385 --> 00:35:57,021
- Detaching them from left caudate lobe.
- Yes.

507
00:36:04,762 --> 00:36:07,031
That's hepatic vein avulsion.

508
00:36:08,232 --> 00:36:09,800
It happened three years ago.

509
00:36:11,369 --> 00:36:13,538
The branch retinal vein is bleeding.

510
00:36:13,971 --> 00:36:16,974
As I expected,
it happened like this...

511
00:36:17,041 --> 00:36:18,276
So?

512
00:36:18,776 --> 00:36:21,612
This is avulsion.
Surly it's bleeding.

513
00:36:21,679 --> 00:36:22,780
Surely?

514
00:36:22,847 --> 00:36:25,349
This is not a mistake.

515
00:36:25,716 --> 00:36:28,019
- You have to sew it up.
- I won't.

516
00:36:28,085 --> 00:36:30,955
- You don't?
- The blood pressure is dropping.

517
00:36:33,524 --> 00:36:34,625
Astriction with gauze.

518
00:36:38,563 --> 00:36:41,532
Move. You go there.

519
00:36:43,167 --> 00:36:44,035
There.

520
00:36:45,703 --> 00:36:46,837
Give it to me.

521
00:36:48,406 --> 00:36:50,608
Switch the damaged area

522
00:36:51,475 --> 00:36:54,245
from a valley to a wall,
then sew it up.

523
00:36:59,250 --> 00:37:02,086
For the last three years,
what have you learned?

524
00:37:13,130 --> 00:37:17,902
Switch the damaged area
from a valley to a wall?

525
00:37:24,308 --> 00:37:28,246
I sew up
the branch retinal vein astriction.

526
00:37:34,318 --> 00:37:37,455
Switch the damaged area...

527
00:37:41,559 --> 00:37:44,962
From a valley to a wall...

528
00:38:00,011 --> 00:38:02,647
Detaching is complete. I sew it up.

529
00:38:02,713 --> 00:38:04,048
- Sutures 5-0.
- Yes.

530
00:38:07,718 --> 00:38:08,853
Forceps.

531
00:38:18,529 --> 00:38:19,730
Metzen.

532
00:38:24,735 --> 00:38:26,737
Suture is complete.
How's the vital?

533
00:38:26,804 --> 00:38:29,440
The blood pressure 110/70,
the heart rate 90.

534
00:38:32,743 --> 00:38:35,379
Proceed detaching caudate lobe.

535
00:38:36,347 --> 00:38:37,915
- Metzen.
- Yes.

536
00:38:49,727 --> 00:38:52,530
- Michiko!
- Don't run in the hallway!

537
00:39:01,572 --> 00:39:03,808
The suture is finished. It's done.

538
00:39:04,542 --> 00:39:07,078
The vital sign is stable.

539
00:39:11,649 --> 00:39:13,150
Good job.

540
00:39:15,252 --> 00:39:16,187
Bye.

541
00:39:16,754 --> 00:39:19,323
- Good job.
- Thanks.

542
00:39:24,128 --> 00:39:25,363
Great job.

543
00:39:29,100 --> 00:39:30,101
Thank you.

544
00:40:02,133 --> 00:40:03,100
Michiko.

545
00:40:03,167 --> 00:40:04,702
Hiruma told me.

546
00:40:04,769 --> 00:40:06,270
What were you thinking?

547
00:40:06,904 --> 00:40:08,372
Darn it, did he tell you?

548
00:40:08,439 --> 00:40:11,308
Are you listening?

549
00:40:13,844 --> 00:40:16,347
We're getting on the elevator.

550
00:40:16,414 --> 00:40:17,915
Don't do that, Michiko!

551
00:40:18,282 --> 00:40:19,483
Hey!

552
00:40:19,884 --> 00:40:21,652
Michiko! Don't do it!

553
00:40:26,457 --> 00:40:27,691
Hello.

554
00:40:28,893 --> 00:40:31,095
Executive Manager Hiruma asked me

555
00:40:31,162 --> 00:40:35,366
to take them here from the airport.

556
00:40:40,004 --> 00:40:41,038
Thank you.

557
00:40:42,706 --> 00:40:43,808
Tired from the long trip?

558
00:40:46,510 --> 00:40:47,344
Are you surprised?

559
00:40:53,117 --> 00:40:53,984
Are you okay?

560
00:40:55,886 --> 00:40:58,656
I didn't know Daimon ever smiles.

561
00:41:04,929 --> 00:41:05,796
How is she?

562
00:41:05,863 --> 00:41:07,264
It's 36.8 degrees C.

563
00:41:09,400 --> 00:41:13,637
I'm so glad. I'm so grateful.

564
00:41:15,673 --> 00:41:20,010
Michiko Daimon must be
the great surgeon.

565
00:41:20,744 --> 00:41:22,279
Michiko Daimon...

566
00:41:24,515 --> 00:41:28,118
She'd become the Double
under one condition;

567
00:41:29,520 --> 00:41:34,592
let her perform surgery on the child
from our branch hospital.

568
00:41:35,926 --> 00:41:38,429
She's really something.

569
00:41:39,063 --> 00:41:40,464
Rather, I'm stunned.

570
00:41:43,100 --> 00:41:44,068
Sir.

571
00:41:47,304 --> 00:41:48,239
It's not like that.

572
00:41:48,639 --> 00:41:49,473
About what?

573
00:41:53,677 --> 00:41:58,115
From the middle to the end,
your daughter's surgery

574
00:42:00,885 --> 00:42:04,221
was done by Dr. Kondo.

575
00:42:05,990 --> 00:42:07,191
What did Daimon do?

576
00:42:11,028 --> 00:42:15,366
She just watched the operation
as his assistant.

577
00:42:17,201 --> 00:42:18,035
Just watched it?

578
00:42:23,941 --> 00:42:26,877
Your surgery will be done here.

579
00:42:29,413 --> 00:42:30,714
You will get well.

580
00:42:32,383 --> 00:42:35,586
And you will be a fisherman
like your dad.

581
00:42:38,022 --> 00:42:38,856
Yeah.

582
00:42:40,558 --> 00:42:41,425
Promise me.

583
00:42:46,196 --> 00:42:47,197
You can draw well.

584
00:42:54,872 --> 00:42:56,140
I told you

585
00:42:57,074 --> 00:43:00,177
I know your skills more than you do.

586
00:43:01,478 --> 00:43:03,514
You can't make it.

587
00:43:03,948 --> 00:43:08,586
You're thinking of exteriorizing
multiple organs and tumor excision.

588
00:43:08,652 --> 00:43:11,422
- Hey, you know it.
- Don't get a swelled head!

589
00:43:12,790 --> 00:43:16,694
Only two cases were successful
in the world.

590
00:43:17,928 --> 00:43:20,230
There is no precedent in Japan.

591
00:43:21,265 --> 00:43:22,232
Michiko,

592
00:43:23,334 --> 00:43:24,568
you can't say,

593
00:43:25,369 --> 00:43:28,539
"I never fail" this time.

594
00:43:30,941 --> 00:43:31,775
Michiko,

595
00:43:33,844 --> 00:43:35,346
I don't want to lose you.

596
00:43:44,054 --> 00:43:45,489
I met the girl...

597
00:43:46,557 --> 00:43:50,995
and found out her disease.
You're telling me to do nothing?

598
00:43:51,061 --> 00:43:53,030
- Should I run?
- That's not my point...

599
00:43:53,097 --> 00:43:54,465
To Kurumi,

600
00:43:55,099 --> 00:43:57,935
the surgery is her last resort.

601
00:44:04,642 --> 00:44:07,511
<i>This is a story</i>
<i>about a maverick female doctor.</i>

602
00:44:10,614 --> 00:44:11,682
REQUEST FORM

603
00:44:18,956 --> 00:44:21,458
They are fooling me.

604
00:44:32,870 --> 00:44:35,506
<i>University hospitals lost</i>
<i>their authorities.</i>

605
00:44:35,572 --> 00:44:37,641
<i>Medical care has become the world</i>

606
00:44:37,941 --> 00:44:41,612
<i>where the strong prey on the weak.</i>

607
00:44:42,913 --> 00:44:47,418
<i>To save this crisis in the world of</i>
<i>medical care, a freelance doctor,</i>

608
00:44:47,484 --> 00:44:51,121
<i>in another word,</i>
<i>a maverick doctor, appeared.</i>

609
00:44:52,856 --> 00:44:55,059
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

610
00:44:56,160 --> 00:44:58,662
<i>She hates groups, authority,</i>

611
00:44:58,729 --> 00:44:59,997
<i>and being controlled.</i>

612
00:45:01,098 --> 00:45:06,270
<i>Her medical certifications</i>
<i>and work experience are her only weapons.</i>

613
00:45:13,877 --> 00:45:15,779
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

614
00:45:16,346 --> 00:45:19,049
<i>also known as Doctor-X.</i>

615
00:46:29,653 --> 00:46:31,922
THE STORY DEPICTED IN THIS DRAMA
IS FICTITIOUS

616
00:46:31,989 --> 00:46:34,024
FINAL EPISODE

617
00:46:34,091 --> 00:46:36,360
I'll make Michiko Daimon fail.

618
00:46:36,426 --> 00:46:38,362
GOODBYE, MICHIKO DAIMON

619
00:46:38,929 --> 00:46:40,397
She only has six months to live.

620
00:46:40,464 --> 00:46:42,533
She never fails.

621
00:46:42,599 --> 00:46:44,601
I won't allow you to do the surgery.

622
00:46:44,668 --> 00:46:46,870
Finally the day you quit is coming.
